<title>CHINA: China Jan cotton imports up 119.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>China Jan cotton imports up 119.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's imports of cotton soared by 119.7 percent to 90,000 tonnes in January from a year-earlier period, the International Business Daily said on Thursday.</p>
<p>China's cotton imports reached 650,000 tonnes in 1996, down by 12.2 percent compared with a year ago, the newspaper quoted customs figures as saying.</p>
<p>Cotton exports in 1996 slumped 79.2 percent to 4,493 tonnes from 21,619 tonnes, the figures showed.</p>
<p>It did not give export figures for January 1997.</p>
</text>
